Specular patch to UnRAR 7.1.0 (vendor/unrar in unrar_sys 0.5.8): handle I/O.

What it changes
  file.hpp, file.cpp, and two early returns in volume.cpp. Adds
  SpecularUnrarSetOpenHook(). When a hook is set, File::Open no longer opens anything by path: it hands the UTF-8 name
  to the hook, which returns an already-open, readable handle (a POSIX file
  descriptor, or a Windows HANDLE) or -1 for "no such file". Such a
  "borrowed" handle is read with positioned reads (pread, or ReadFile with
  an OVERLAPPED offset) from a position kept in the File object, seeks only
  move that 64-bit position (overflow-checked; seeking past the end is
  allowed and reads 0 bytes there), Tell returns it, and Close never closes
  it, because the caller owns it. File::Create always fails while a hook is
  set, and write/update opens are refused. Without a hook UnRAR behaves
  exactly as upstream. With a hook set, the DLL volume callbacks
  (UCM_CHANGEVOLUME[W], ChangeVolProc) are not called: the hook is how the
  embedding program learns of and supplies each volume, so a volume the hook
  cannot open is final (ERAR_EOPEN). Decompression code is not touched.

Why
  Specular runs UnRAR in a sandboxed decode host that cannot open user
  files (on Windows an AppContainer without file-system access; on Linux
  and macOS a seccomp/Landlock or Seatbelt profile without open()). The
  unsandboxed app opens each archive volume read-only and passes the handle
  in (DuplicateHandle on Windows, SCM_RIGHTS on Unix). Multi-volume names
  that UnRAR asks for go through the same hook, which asks the app.

How it is applied
  build.rs copies vendor/unrar to OUT_DIR and applies this file there with
  an exact-context unified-diff applier that fails the build if any hunk
  does not match. The vendored sources themselves stay pristine. Everything
  above the first "--- " line is ignored by the applier.

